Package: khmd
Title: Read Explicit CSV Observation Releases for Housing Research
Version: 0.0.5
Authors@R: person("Jinhyeok", "Jang", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "jedjang1@gmail.com")
Description: Opens explicit CSV source release manifests and reads external
    SQLite observation stores without rewriting source data. Provides bounded
    retrieval, chunk callbacks, provenance inspection and occurrence counts.
    Reads separately versioned sparse grid observation panels and query-region
    assignment quality denominators with explicit source and grid bindings.
    Reads exact reported-value price and rent descriptive statistics with
    metric-specific valid denominators and explicit rental subtype levels.
    Preserves raw values and observability states and does not assert unique
    transaction identity, historical spatial boundaries or population completeness.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: DBI, RSQLite (>= 2.2.17), jsonlite, digest
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
